{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FGhgr9QNEuKeVcwkRXCduk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation: web ui: dashboard\n2\t\n3\t## Summary\n4\t\n5\tAdded a default dashboard view to the web UI, rendered at `#/` (root) and\n6\treachable via the \"manigot\" brand link in the top-left, per the brief. The\n7\tdashboard shows an overview across every registered project: aggregate\n8\tcounts (projects, open jobs, needs-human, running), an attention-sorted list\n9\tof jobs needing attention across all projects, and a projects grid linking\n10\tinto each project's jobs view.\n11\t\n12\t## Changes\n13\t\n14\tTASK-1: Added `web-ui/src/lib/views/DashboardView.svelte` (new view) and\n15\t`web-ui/src/lib/dashboard.ts` (pure aggregation logic, factored out for\n16\ttestability). The view loads `api.getProjects()` once on mount, then fans\n17\tout one `api.getJobs(project)` call per project via `Promise.allSettled` —\n18\ta per-project failure degrades to an inline \"couldn't load jobs for X\" note\n19\tin that project's card rather than blanking the page. `dashboard.ts`\n20\texports `aggregateCounts()` and `attentionJobs()`, both built on `stage.ts`'s\n21\texisting `attention()`/`sortByAttention()`. No polling beyond the initial\n22\tload, to avoid a request storm as the project registry grows. Styled to\n23\tmatch the existing view conventions (`.page` layout, `--r-*`/`--ink-*`/\n24\t`--bg-*` tokens).\n25\t\n26\tTASK-2: Wired the dashboard into `web-ui/src/App.svelte`: imported\n27\t`DashboardView` and added a route branch rendering it when\n28\t`route.name === 'home'` and the daemon is connected with a loaded, non-empty\n29\tproject list. Removed the `$effect` that previously force-navigated `home`\n30\t→ `jobs/<active>` whenever a project was active — `#/` and the brand link\n31\tnow land on the dashboard instead of auto-redirecting. The existing\n32\tdown/no-projects/connecting/error landing states are untouched (same\n33\ttrailing `{:else}` branch, now only reached when the dashboard's condition\n34\tdoesn't hold).\n35\t\n36\tTASK-3: Rewrote the `App.test.ts` regression test that asserted the old\n37\tauto-redirect behavior. It now asserts the dashboard renders at `#/` (hash\n38\tstays `#/`, `.landing` is gone, `h1` reads \"Dashboard\") and preserves the\n39\toriginal double-hash regression guard by driving the project-switch path\n40\t(`navigate(href(...))` via the project `<select>`) and confirming the hash\n41\tlands as a single `#/p/manigot`, not `##/p/manigot`.\n42\t\n43\tTASK-4: Added test coverage for the new behavior: a focused `App.test.ts`\n44\tcase rendering the dashboard with two projects and jobs in various\n45\tstates, asserting the attention list and projects grid render correctly;\n46\tand a new `web-ui/src/lib/dashboard.test.ts` unit-testing `aggregateCounts()`\n47\tand `attentionJobs()` (counting, skipping failed per-project loads, sorting\n48\tby attention, tagging jobs with their project) — following `stage.test.ts`'s\n49\tpattern.\n50\t\n51\tTASK-5: Updated `web-ui/README.md`'s `Layout` section to list\n52\t`DashboardView` alongside the other views.\n53\t\n54\t## Verification\n55\t\n56\t- `npm run build` — clean production build, no new warnings.\n57\t- `npm test` — full suite (93 tests across 13 files) passes.\n58\t- Rendered the dashboard with `shot` against the mock backend\n59\t  (`npm run dev:mock`) at 375px and 1280px — layout, contrast (WCAG AA),\n60\t  and attention-list/project-grid content all correct; screenshots and the\n61\t  render report are committed under `screenshots/`.\n62\t\n63\t## Known issues / follow-ups\n64\t\n65\tNone.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"922db0ba-8634-4cea-a4ec-b27bd027a32b","uuid":"88d15f94-0757-4a07-9c12-81f692afd663","timestamp":"2026-08-29T12:58:17.652Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/of_web-ui-dashboard/implementation.md","content":"# Implementation: web ui: dashboard\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a default dashboard view to the web UI, rendered at `#/` (root) and\nreachable via the \"manigot\" brand link in the top-left, per the brief. The\ndashboard shows an overview across every registered project: aggregate\ncounts (projects, open jobs, needs-human, running), an attention-sorted list\nof jobs needing attention across all projects, and a projects grid linking\ninto each project's jobs view.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: Added `web-ui/src/lib/views/DashboardView.svelte` (new view) and\n`web-ui/src/lib/dashboard.ts` (pure aggregation logic, factored out for\ntestability). The view loads `api.getProjects()` once on mount, then fans\nout one `api.getJobs(project)` call per project via `Promise.allSettled` —\na per-project failure degrades to an inline \"couldn't load jobs for X\" note\nin that project's card rather than blanking the page. `dashboard.ts`\nexports `aggregateCounts()` and `attentionJobs()`, both built on `stage.ts`'s\nexisting `attention()`/`sortByAttention()`. No polling beyond the initial\nload, to avoid a request storm as the project registry grows. Styled to\nmatch the existing view conventions (`.page` layout, `--r-*`/`--ink-*`/\n`--bg-*` tokens).\n\nTASK-2: Wired the dashboard into `web-ui/src/App.svelte`: imported\n`DashboardView` and added a route branch rendering it when\n`route.name === 'home'` and the daemon is connected with a loaded, non-empty\nproject list. Removed the `$effect` that previously force-navigated `home`\n→ `jobs/<active>` whenever a project was active — `#/` and the brand link\nnow land on the dashboard instead of auto-redirecting. The existing\ndown/no-projects/connecting/error landing states are untouched (same\ntrailing `{:else}` branch, now only reached when the dashboard's condition\ndoesn't hold).\n\nTASK-3: Rewrote the `App.test.ts` regression test that asserted the old\nauto-redirect behavior. It now asserts the dashboard renders at `#/` (hash\nstays `#/`, `.landing` is gone, `h1` reads \"Dashboard\") and preserves the\noriginal double-hash regression guard by driving the project-switch path\n(`navigate(href(...))` via the project `<select>`) and confirming the hash\nlands as a single `#/p/manigot`, not `##/p/manigot`.\n\nTASK-4: Added test coverage for the new behavior: a focused `App.test.ts`\ncase rendering the dashboard with two projects and jobs in various\nstates, asserting the attention list and projects grid render correctly;\nand a new `web-ui/src/lib/dashboard.test.ts` unit-testing `aggregateCounts()`\nand `attentionJobs()` (counting, skipping failed per-project loads, sorting\nby attention, tagging jobs with their project) — following `stage.test.ts`'s\npattern.\n\nTASK-5: Updated `web-ui/README.md`'s `Layout` section to list\n`DashboardView` alongside the other views.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npm run build` — clean production build, no new warnings.\n- `npm test` — full suite (93 tests across 13 files) passes.\n- Rendered the dashboard with `shot` against the mock backend\n  (`npm run dev:mock`) at 375px and 1280px — layout, contrast (WCAG AA),\n  and attention-list/project-grid content all correct; screenshots and the\n  render report are committed under `screenshots/`.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\nNone.\n","numLines":66,"startLine":1,"totalLines":66}}}
